###### Subsection 3: Suspended sentence with probation

###### Paragraph 1: Conditions for granting suspended sentence with probation

###### Article 132

35: The court that pronounces a term of imprisonment may, under the conditions provided below, order that its execution be suspended, with the convicted natural person being placed under the probation regime.

Suspended sentence with probation is applicable to sentences of imprisonment pronounced for common law crimes or offences.

In this case, the Court may declare the execution of the sentence provisionally.

It sets the probation period which may not be less than three years nor more than five years, as well as the probationary tests assigned to the convicted person.

After pronouncing the imprisonment with suspended sentence with probation, the president of the court notifies the convicted person, when present, of the obligations to be respected during the suspended sentence with probation and warns of the consequences that would result from a conviction for a new offence committed during the probation period or a breach of the control measures and particular obligations imposed. The president informs the convicted person of the possibility of having the conviction declared null and void if satisfactory conduct is observed.

###### Article 132

36: When a conviction is accompanied by suspended sentence with probation, the convicted person is placed under the supervision of the sentence enforcement judge or, failing that, the public prosecutor in whose jurisdiction the convicted person has habitual residence or, if the convicted person has no residence in Mali, under the supervision of the sentence enforcement judge or, failing that, the public prosecutor of the court that pronounced the conviction.

If the acts necessary for the execution of the probationary measures must be carried out outside the limits of that jurisdiction, the sentence enforcement judge or, failing that, the public prosecutor instructs the territorially competent counterpart to oversee them.

###### Paragraph 2: Probation regime

###### Article 132

37: During the probation period, the convicted person must comply with the control measures provided for in Article 132-38 below and with those particular obligations provided for in Article 132-39 below that are specifically imposed. In addition, the convicted person may benefit from assistance measures intended to promote social rehabilitation.

These measures and particular obligations cease to apply and the probation period is suspended during the time the convicted person is incarcerated.

###### Article 132

38: The control measures to which the convicted person must submit are as follows:

1°) respond to summonses from the sentence enforcement judge or the designated social worker;

2°) receive visits from the social worker and provide information or documents that enable verification of means of subsistence and execution of obligations;

3°) notify the social worker of changes of employment;

4°) notify the social worker of changes of residence or any travel exceeding fifteen days and report the return;

5°) obtain prior authorization from the sentence enforcement judge for any change of employment or residence, when such change is likely to obstruct the execution of obligations;

6°) inform the sentence enforcement judge in advance of any travel abroad.

###### Article 132

39: The sentencing court or the sentence enforcement judge may specifically impose on the convicted person compliance with one or more of the following obligations:

1°) engage in professional activity or pursue education or vocational training;

2°) establish residence in a specified place;

3°) submit to medical examination, treatment or care measures, even under hospitalization. These measures may consist of a therapeutic injunction when it appears that the convicted person uses narcotics or habitually and excessively consumes alcoholic beverages;

4°) prove contribution to family expenses or regular payment of maintenance for which the convicted person is liable;

5°) make reparation in whole or in part, according to contributory capacity, for damages caused by the offence, even in the absence of a decision on the civil action;

6°) prove payment according to contributory capacity of sums owed to the Public Treasury following the conviction;

7°) refrain from driving certain vehicles determined by the licence categories provided for in the Highway Code;

8°) not engage in the activity in the exercise of or on the occasion of the exercise of which the offence was committed or not engage in an activity involving habitual contact with minors;

9°) refrain from appearing in any place, any category of places or any specifically designated area;

10°) not place bets, particularly with mutual betting organizations, and not take part in games of money and chance;

11°) not frequent drinking establishments;

12°) not associate with certain convicted persons, particularly the perpetrators or accomplices of the offence;

13°) refrain from entering into contact with certain persons, including the victim, or certain categories of persons, and particularly minors, except, where applicable, those designated by the court;

14°) not possess or carry a weapon;

15°) in case of an offence committed either against the spouse, or against the children of the convicted person or those of the spouse, reside outside the domicile or residence of the couple and, where applicable, refrain from appearing at that domicile or residence or in the immediate vicinity thereof, as well as, if necessary, undergo health, social or psychological care; these provisions are also applicable when the offence is committed by the former spouse of the victim, the domicile concerned being then that of the victim. For the application of this paragraph, the victim's opinion is obtained, as soon as possible and by all means, on the appropriateness of requiring the convicted person to reside outside the couple's dwelling. Except in special circumstances, this measure is taken when acts of violence likely to be repeated are involved and the victim requests it. The court may specify the terms for covering the costs relating to this accommodation;

16°) obtain prior authorization from the sentence enforcement judge for any travel abroad.

###### Paragraph 3: Revocation of suspended sentence with probation

###### Article 132

40: Suspended sentence with probation may be revoked by the trial court under the conditions provided for in Article 132-41 below.
It may also be revoked by the sentence enforcement judge when the convicted person has not complied with the control measures and particular obligations imposed. Any breach of these measures and obligations committed after the probation has become enforceable may justify revocation of the suspended sentence. If this revocation is ordered while the conviction has not yet acquired a final character, it becomes null and void in the event that this conviction is subsequently reversed or annulled.

