#### Chapter 2: Espionage

###### Article 222

1: Is guilty of espionage and punished by death, any foreigner who commits one of the acts referred to in articles 221-1 paragraphs 2, 3, 4 above and 221-2 paragraphs 1°, 2° and 3° above.

The provocation to commit or the offer to commit one of the crimes referred to in articles 221-1 and 221-2 above and in this article is punished as the crime itself.

###### Article 222

2: Are deemed national defense secrets for the application of this Code:
1°) information of a military, diplomatic, economic or industrial nature which, by its nature, must be known only to persons qualified to hold it, and must, in the interest of national defense, be kept secret from any other person;
2°) objects, materials, writings, drawings, plans, maps, photographs or other reproductions, and all other documents whatsoever which, by their nature, must be known only to persons qualified to handle or hold them, and must be kept secret from any other person, which may lead to the discovery of information belonging to one of the categories referred to in the preceding paragraph;

3°) military information of any nature, not made public by the Government and not included in the above enumerations, the publication, dissemination, disclosure or reproduction of which is prohibited by a law or by a decree;

4°) information relating to measures taken to discover and arrest the perpetrators and accomplices of crimes or offenses against the security of the State.

#### Chapter 3: Other offenses against the external security of the State

###### Article 223

1: Is guilty of an offense against the external security of the State and punished by the penalties provided for in article 223-5 below any Malian or any foreigner:

1°) who, by hostile acts not approved by the Government, exposes Mali to a declaration of war;

2°) who, by acts not approved by the Government, exposes Malians to suffer reprisals;

3°) who, in time of peace, enlists soldiers on behalf of a foreign power, in Malian territory;

4°) who, in time of war, knowingly maintains, without authorization from the Government, correspondence or relations with the subjects or agents of an enemy power;

5°) who, in time of war, in defiance of enacted prohibitions, carries out directly or through an intermediary, acts of commerce with the subjects or agents of an enemy power.

###### Article 223

2: Is guilty of an offense against the external security of the State and punished by the penalties provided for in article 223-5 below any Malian or any foreigner:

1°) who undertakes, by any means whatsoever, to undermine the integrity of Malian territory;
2°) who maintains with the agents of a foreign power intelligence having as its object or having as its effect to harm the military or diplomatic situation of Mali.

###### Article 223

3: Is guilty of an offense against the external security of the State and punished by the penalties provided for in article 223-5 below any Malian or foreigner:

1°) who, for a purpose other than that of delivering it to a foreign power or its agents, or secures being without qualification by any means whatsoever, possession of a national defense secret, or knowingly and without qualification holds an object or document deemed a national defense secret, or which may lead to the discovery of such a secret, or brings said secret, in any form and by any means whatsoever, to the knowledge of the public or of a qualified person;

2°) who, through imprudence, negligence or non-observance of regulations, allows to be destroyed, removed or taken away, in whole or in part, and even momentarily, objects, materials, documents or information entrusted to him, and knowledge of which may lead to the discovery of a national defense secret or allows knowledge, copy or reproduction thereof to be taken, even in part;

3°) who, without prior authorization from the competent authority, delivers or communicates to a person acting on behalf of a power or a foreign enterprise, either an invention of interest to national defense, or information, studies or manufacturing processes relating to an invention of this kind, or to an industrial application of interest to national defense.

###### Article 223

4: Is also guilty of an offense against the external security of the State, and punished by the same penalties, without prejudice if applicable, to the penalties provided for the attempt of the crimes provided for in articles 221-1 and 221-2 of this Code, any Malian or any foreigner:

1°) who enters, under a disguise or a false name, or by concealing his quality, or his nationality in a fortress, a work, post or arsenal, in the works, camps, bivouacs or cantonments of an army, in a warship, or a merchant ship employed for national defense, in a military establishment of any nature, or in an establishment or shipyard working for national defense;

2°) who, even without disguising himself or without concealing his name, his quality or his nationality organizes in a covert manner any means of correspondence or remote transmission likely to harm national defense;

3°) who flies over Malian territory by means of a foreign aircraft without being authorized to do so by a diplomatic convention or permission from the Malian authority;

4°) who, in a prohibited zone fixed by the military authority executes without the authorization thereof drawings, photographs, surveys or topographical operations inside or around places, works, posts or military and maritime establishments;

5°) who stays, in defiance of an enacted regulatory prohibition, within a determined radius around fortified works or military and maritime establishments.

###### Article 223

5: If they are committed in time of war, offenses against the external security of the State are punished by imprisonment for twenty years.

If they are committed in time of peace, they are punished by imprisonment of five years and a fine of 1,600,000 francs.

However, the imprisonment may be increased to ten years and the fine to 3,600,000 francs with regard to the offenses referred to in articles 223-1 paragraph 1, 223-2 paragraph 1 and 223-3 above.

In time of war, all other acts, knowingly accomplished, of a nature to harm national defense, are punished, if they are not already by another text, by imprisonment of five years and a fine of 1,600,000 francs.

In all cases, the guilty parties may in addition be deprived for twenty years of the rights mentioned in article 131-6 of this Code. They may also be subject to a prohibition of residence of twenty years.

The attempt of the offense is punished as the offense itself.

The offense committed abroad is punished as the offense committed in Malian territory.

###### Article 223

6: The confiscation of the object of the crime or offense and of the objects and instruments having served to commit it is automatic, without there being any need to investigate whether or not they belong to the convicted persons.

The remuneration received by the guilty party, or the amount of its value when the remuneration could not be seized, are declared acquired by the Public Treasury by the judgment.

For the application of the penalty and the regime of provisional detention, crimes and offenses against the external security of the State are considered as crimes and offenses of common law.

