###### Article 242

29: [Law No. 01-077 of 18 July 2001 establishing the general rules of construction]:

Is punished by one year's imprisonment and a fine of 1,000,000 francs, anyone who:

1°) uses non-regulated construction materials, products or components, in violation of the rules for the use of construction materials, products and components;

2°) uses construction techniques provided for by law without the required authorizations and approvals;

3°) does not engage a company for the execution of a construction requiring a company, in violation of paragraph 1 of Article 242-26 above;

4°) executes himself or with the help of acquaintances demolition works requiring authorization in violation of paragraph 2 of Article 242-26 above;
In case of recidivism, the maximum penalty is applied;

5°) undertakes or establishes a construction without a building permit in violation of Article 242-27 above.

In the event that the construction does not conform to the vocation of the land, in addition to the above-mentioned sanctions, the construction is entirely demolished;

6°) in violation of the specific rules applicable to the construction and operation of assembly establishments, established by decree taken in the Council of Ministers:

a)	smokes, uses open fire or keeps flammable liquids in the specified places;

b)	smokes, uses open fire, in particular matches and lighters or uses cooking appliances in the projection booth for Celluloid films;

c)	does not suspend the operation of the assembly establishment in case of failure of an installation, equipment or device necessary for safety;

7°) in violation of the specific rules applicable to the construction and operation of hospital establishments, established by decree taken in the Council of Ministers:

a)	does not carry out inspections or does not carry them out on time;

b)	does not repair the defects noted by experts during inspections;

8°) in violation of the specific rules applicable to the construction and operation of educational establishments, established by decree taken in the Council of Ministers:

a)	does not carry out inspections or does not carry them out on time;

b)	does not repair the defects noted by experts during inspections;

c)	uses open fire in inappropriate rooms and without permanent supervision;

d)	does not maintain and regularly inspect technical installations and equipment;

e)	does not keep fire extinguishers ready in rooms with a high risk of fire.

9°) in violation of the specific rules applicable to the construction and operation of catering and accommodation establishments, established by decree taken in the Council of Ministers:

a)	does not have the prescribed inspections carried out or does not have them carried out on time;

b)	does not repair the defects noted;

10°) in violation of the specific rules applicable to the construction and operation of commercial establishments, established by decree taken in the Council of Ministers:

c)	smokes or uses an open fire;

d)	uses electric radiant cookers;

e)	carries out welding work or similar fire work without supervision of the fire safety service.

###### Article 242

30: Is punished by two years' imprisonment and a fine of 2,000,000 francs, any person who, despite sufficient knowledge, makes false declarations or submits false documents to obtain or prevent the execution of an administrative act issued in accordance with this paragraph.

In case of recidivism, the maximum penalty is always applied.

The Court may, in addition, order the total or partial demolition of the constructions.

###### Article 242

31: [Law No. 02-016 of 03 June 2002, establishing the general rules of urban planning]:

Any person who carries out or undertakes, has carried out or has undertaken constructions or installations in a subdivided zone without prior authorization from the administration or in violation of the legislative and regulatory provisions in force, is punished by a fine of 2,000,000 francs.

This fine is calculated according to the state of progress of the works.

Architects, contractors or any other person having contributed to the execution of said constructions or installations, are punished by the same penalties.

###### Article 242

32: [Law No. 02-016 of 03 June 2002, establishing the general rules of urban planning]:

Any person who divides a property for family use in a subdivided zone without prior authorization from the administration, is punished by a fine of 50,000 francs per parcel resulting from the division.

Any person who divides a property other than family property in a subdivided zone without prior authorization from the Administration is punished by a fine of 1,000,000 francs per parcel resulting from the division;

###### Article 242

33: [Law No. 02-016 of 03 June 2002, establishing the general rules of Urban Planning]:

Without prejudice to the sanctions provided for by other legislative and regulatory texts, any person who subdivides a property in a subdivided zone without having obtained prior administrative authorization, is punished by six months' imprisonment and a fine of 2,000,000 francs per parcel resulting from the subdivision.

The Court may, upon request of the Administration, order for all offences referred to in this chapter, the demolition of constructions erected in violation of the applicable provisions and the restoration of the premises at the expense of the offender.

##### Section 4

Acts of obstruction to Justice Paragraph 1: Obstruction of recourse to Justice

###### Article 242

34: Any threat or any other act of intimidation towards anyone, committed with a view to inducing the victim of a crime or an offence not to file a complaint or to retract, is punished by five years' imprisonment and a fine of 1,000,000 francs.

###### Article 242

35: The act of anyone having knowledge of a crime whose effects can still be prevented or limited, or whose perpetrators are likely to commit new crimes that could be prevented, of not informing the judicial or administrative authorities is punished by the penalties provided for in the preceding article.

Are exempted from the preceding provisions, except with regard to terrorist acts and crimes committed against minors:

1°) relatives in the direct line and their spouses, as well as brothers and sisters and their spouses, of the perpetrator or accomplice of the crime;

2°) the spouse of the perpetrator or accomplice of the crime, or the person who notoriously lives in a marital situation with him.
Also exempted from the provisions of the first paragraph are persons bound to secrecy under the conditions provided for in Article 322-2 of this Code.

###### Paragraph 2: Obstruction of the proper functioning of justice

###### Article 242

36: Is punished by five years' imprisonment and a fine of 1,000,000 francs anyone who:
1°) resorts to physical force, threats or intimidation or promises to offer or grant an undue advantage to obtain false testimony or prevent testimony or the presentation of evidence in a proceeding;
2°) resorts to physical force, threats or intimidation to prevent an officer of justice or an officer of the detection and law enforcement services from exercising the duties of his office.

