###### Article 243

2 : For the purposes of this Code, the following terms mean:

1°) competent authorities: bodies which, by virtue of a legal or regulatory provision, are empowered to perform or order the acts or measures provided for by the uniform law relating to counterfeiting;

2°) BCEAO or Central Bank: the Central Bank of West African States;

3°) counterfeiting: the manufacture of a monetary sign imitating a monetary sign issued by the BCEAO or any other authorized foreign issuing institution;

4°) foreigner: any person who lives in the Union without having the nationality of one of the Member States of UMOA;

5°) falsification: the alteration of a monetary sign with a view to modifying its substance or weight;

6°) counterfeit currency, counterfeit banknotes or counterfeit coins: banknotes and coins which have the appearance of banknotes or coins issued by the BCEAO or any other authorized foreign issuing body or, although intended to be put into circulation, have not yet been issued by the institutions authorized for this purpose;

7°) counterfeiting:

a)	all fraudulent acts, counterfeiting and falsification of manufacture or alteration of monetary signs issued by the BCEAO or any other authorized foreign issuing institution, for this purpose, whatever the means employed to produce the result;

b)	the putting into circulation of counterfeit currency with full knowledge;

c)	the act of holding, importing, exporting, transporting, receiving or obtaining counterfeit currency, with the intention of putting it into circulation with full knowledge;

d)	the fraudulent act of manufacturing, holding, receiving or obtaining instruments, objects, computer programs or any other process intended, by their nature, for the manufacture of counterfeit currency, the alteration of currencies or the manufacture of security elements of monetary signs;

8°) FCFA: Franc of the African Financial Community;

9°) putting counterfeit currency into circulation: the issuance of counterfeit currency, regardless of the number of banknotes or coins circulated;

10°) reproduction of monetary signs: creation of any tangible or intangible image which bears a resemblance to a banknote or the image of a coin, whatever the size of the image, the materials, instruments and techniques used to produce it and regardless of whether the patterns, letters and symbols appearing on the monetary sign have been modified or not;

11°) monetary signs: banknotes or coins having or having had legal tender;

12°) UMOA or Union: West African Monetary Union.

###### Paragraphe 2 : Des incriminations et des peines applicables

###### Article 243

3 : The counterfeiting or falsification of banknotes or coins having legal tender in the national territory of a Member State of UMOA or abroad is punished by twenty years' imprisonment and a fine equal to ten times the value of said signs without being less than 20,000,000 francs.

The counterfeiting or falsification of banknotes or coins which, although intended to be put into circulation, have not yet been issued by the institutions authorized for this purpose is punished by the same penalties.
If the offender benefits from mitigating circumstances, the penalty may not be less than five years' imprisonment and a fine of 5,000,000 francs.
Suspension of sentence may not be granted.

###### Article 243

4 : The custodial sentence provided for in the first two paragraphs of the preceding article is accompanied by a safety period of seven years.
During the safety period, the convicted person may not benefit from provisions relating to the method of adjusting sentences, in particular those concerning the suspension or splitting of the sentence, external placement, leave permits, semi-liberty and conditional release.

###### Article 243

5 : The counterfeiting or falsification of banknotes or coins having had legal tender in the national territory or abroad, is punished by five years' imprisonment and a fine equal to ten times the value of said signs, without being less than 2,000,000 francs.

###### Article 243

6 : The manufacture of banknotes and coins carried out using authorized installations or equipment intended for this purpose, when it is carried out in violation of the conditions set by the institutions authorized to issue these monetary signs and without their agreement, is punished by the penalties provided for in Article 243-3 above.

###### Article 243

7 : The putting into circulation, use, display, distribution, importation, exportation, transport, receipt, possession, with full knowledge, of counterfeit or falsified monetary signs having legal tender, is punished by seven years' imprisonment and a fine equal to ten times the value of said signs without being less than 5,000,000 francs.

When they are committed by an organized gang, the offences provided for in the preceding paragraph are punished by the penalties provided for in Article 243-3 above.

The putting into circulation, use, display, distribution, importation, exportation, transport, receipt, possession, of counterfeit or falsified monetary signs having had legal tender, with full knowledge, is punished by three years' imprisonment and a fine equal to ten times the value of said signs, without being less than 1,000,000 francs.

When they are committed by an organized gang, the offences provided for in paragraph 3 of this article are punished by the penalties provided for in Article 243-5 above.

###### Article 243

8 : Those who, having received monetary signs believing them to be good and who, after having discovered their defects, knowingly keep them and refrain from handing them over to the BCEAO or to the competent authorities, are punished by a fine equal to ten times their value, without the amount of the fine being less than 250,000 francs.

Credit institutions, decentralized financial systems, authorized manual exchange dealers and postal financial services which, having received counterfeit or falsified monetary signs during operations with their customers, have not retained them, against receipt, for the purpose of handing them over to the BCEAO or to the competent authorities, are punished by a fine equal to ten times their value, without the amount being less than 2,000,000 francs.

###### Article 243

9 : The putting back into circulation, after having discovered the defects, of counterfeit or falsified banknotes which were believed to be good at the time of receipt, is punished by five years' imprisonment and a fine equal to ten times the value of said signs without being less than 500,000 francs.

###### Article 243

10 : The manufacture, offer, receipt, importation, exportation, or possession, without authorization, of marks, materials, apparatus, instruments, computer programs, or any other element specially intended for the manufacture or protection against counterfeiting or falsification of banknotes or coins is punished by seven years' imprisonment and a fine of 10,000,000 francs.

