7: Are punished by imprisonment of four years and a fine of 3,000,000 francs, the persons and directors or agents of the natural or legal persons referred to in Articles 5 and 6 of the uniform law on the fight against money laundering and the financing of terrorism, when the latter have intentionally:

1°) made to the owner of the sums or to the perpetrator of the acts referred to in Article 8 of the said law, disclosures concerning the declaration they are required to make or concerning the action taken thereon or failed to make the suspicious transaction report provided for in Article 79 of the said law, including in the context of attempted suspicious transactions or made a late declaration;

2°) destroyed or removed documents or records relating to the operations and transactions referred to in Articles 32, 33, 35 and 37 to 40 of the said law;

3°) carried out or attempted to carry out under a false identity one of the operations referred to in the provisions of Articles 18 and 21, 26 to 34, 36, 38 to 40 and 50 to 58 of the said law;

4°) informed, by any means, the person or persons subject to the investigation conducted for acts of financing of terrorism of which they became aware, by reason of their profession or their functions;

5°) made false declarations or communications when carrying out one of the operations referred to in the provisions of Articles 24 to 39 of the said law;

6°) communicated information or documents to persons other than the judicial authorities, State agents responsible for the detection and prosecution of offences related to the financing of terrorism, acting within the framework of a judicial mandate, the supervisory authorities and the National Financial Intelligence Unit (CENTIF);

7°) contravened the obligations to implement administrative freezing measures.

Are punished by a fine of 1,500,000 francs, the persons and directors or agents of the natural or legal persons referred to in Articles 5 and 6 of the said law, when the latter have unintentionally:

1°) failed to make the suspicious transaction report provided for in Article 79 of the said law;

2°) contravened the due diligence and suspicious transaction reporting obligations imposed on them by the provisions of this title.

##### Section 6

Optional additional criminal sanctions incurred by natural persons

###### Article 257

8: Natural persons guilty of the offences defined in Articles 257-1 and 257-5 of this title may also incur the following additional penalties:

1°) permanent banishment from the national territory or for a period of seven years, pronounced against any convicted foreigner;

2°) prohibition from residing, for a period of seven years, in certain administrative districts;

3°) prohibition from leaving the national territory and withdrawal of passport, for a period of five years;

4°) prohibition from exercising civil and political rights, for a period of five years;

5°) prohibition from driving motorized land, sea and air vehicles and withdrawal of permits or licenses, for a period of ten years;

6°) permanent prohibition or for a period of ten years from exercising the profession or activity in connection with which the offence was committed and prohibition from exercising a public function;

7°) prohibition from issuing cheques other than those which allow the withdrawal of funds by the drawer from the drawee or those which are certified and prohibition from using payment cards for a period of five to ten years;

8°) prohibition from holding or carrying a weapon subject to authorization for a period of ten years;

9°) confiscation of all or part of the lawfully acquired property of the convicted person;

10°) confiscation of the property or thing which was used or intended to commit the offence or of the thing which is the proceeds thereof, with the exception of objects capable of restitution.

###### Article 257

9: No sanction pronounced for an offence of financing of terrorism may be accompanied by a suspended sentence.

##### Section 7: Criminal sanctions incurred by legal persons

###### Article 257

10: Legal persons other than the State, on behalf of or for the benefit of which an offence of financing of terrorism or one of the related offences has been committed by one of their organs or representatives, are punished by a fine at a rate equal to five times that incurred by natural persons, without prejudice to the conviction of the latter as perpetrators or accomplices of the same acts.

Legal persons other than the State may, in addition, be sentenced to one or more of the following penalties:

1°) exclusion from public contracts, permanently or for a period of up to ten years;

2°) confiscation of the property which was used or intended to commit the offence or of the property which is the proceeds thereof;

3°) placement under judicial supervision, for a period of up to five years;

4°) prohibition, permanently or for a period of up to ten years, from exercising directly or indirectly one or more professional or social activities in connection with which the offence was committed;

5°) permanent closure or for a period of up to ten years of the establishments or one of the establishments of the enterprise having been used to commit the incriminated acts;

6°) dissolution, when they were created to commit the incriminated acts;

7°) posting of the decision pronounced or dissemination thereof, by the written press or by any audiovisual means of communication, at the expense of the convicted legal person.

The sanctions provided for in points 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 of the second paragraph of this article are not applicable to financial institutions subject to a supervisory authority having disciplinary power.

The competent supervisory authority, referred to by the public prosecutor of any prosecution initiated against a financial institution, may take appropriate sanctions, in accordance with the specific legislative and regulatory texts in force.

##### Section 8: Grounds for exemption from criminal sanctions

###### Article 257

11: Any person guilty, on the one hand, of participation in an association or agreement, with a view to committing one of the offences provided for in this chapter and, on the other hand, of aiding, inciting or advising a natural or legal person with a view to executing them or facilitating their execution, is exempted from criminal sanctions if, having disclosed the existence of this agreement, association, aid or advice to the judicial authority, they thereby enable, on the one hand, the identification of the other persons involved and, on the other hand, the prevention of the commission of the offences of money laundering and financing of terrorism.

##### Section 9: Grounds for mitigation of criminal sanctions

###### Article 257

12: The penalties incurred by any person, perpetrator or accomplice of one of the offences provided for in this chapter who, before any prosecution, enables or facilitates the identification of the other guilty parties or after the initiation of prosecution, enables or facilitates the arrest of the latter, are reduced by half. In addition, the said person is exempted from the fine and, where applicable, from the accessory measures and optional additional penalties.

In matters of financing of terrorism, when the penalty incurred is life imprisonment, it is reduced to twenty years.

##### Section 10

Mandatory confiscation of funds and other financial resources linked to the financing of terrorism

