###### Article 322

18 : Whoever, outside the cases provided for by law, stores or keeps on computer media or memory, without the express consent of the person concerned, personal data which, directly or indirectly, reveal racial or ethnic origin, political, philosophical or religious opinions, or trade union membership, or which relate to the health or sexual life of that person, as well as data relating to offences, convictions or security measures concerning him or her, is punished by imprisonment for five years and a fine of 5,000,000 francs.

###### Article 322

19 : In the case of processing of personal data for the purpose of research in the field of health, whoever carries out processing is punished by imprisonment for five years and a fine of 5,000,000 francs:

1°) without having previously informed the persons concerned individually of their right of access, rectification and opposition, of the nature of the data transmitted and the recipients thereof, as well as the provisions made for their processing, storage and protection;

2°) despite the opposition of the person concerned or, where provided for by law, in the absence of the informed and express consent of the person, or if it concerns a deceased person, despite the refusal expressed by that person during his or her lifetime.

###### Article 322

20 : The act of keeping personal data beyond the period provided for by law or regulation, by the request for authorization or opinion, or by the prior declaration sent to the Personal Data Protection Authority, is punished by imprisonment for five years and a fine of 5,000,000 francs, unless such storage is carried out for historical, statistical or scientific purposes under the conditions provided for by law.

The same penalties apply to the act, outside the cases provided for by law, of processing for purposes other than historical, statistical or scientific purposes personal data kept beyond the period mentioned in the first paragraph.

###### Article 322

21 : Whoever, holding personal data on the occasion of their recording, classification, transmission or any form of processing, diverts such information from its purpose as defined by the legislative provision, regulatory act or decision of the Personal Data Protection Authority authorizing the processing, or by the prior declarations for the implementation of such processing, is punished by imprisonment for five years and a fine of 5,000,000 francs.

###### Article 322

22 : Whoever collects, on the occasion of their recording, classification, transmission or another form of processing, personal data the disclosure of which would have the effect of damaging the reputation of the person concerned or the privacy of his or her private life, brings, without the authorization of the person concerned, such data to the knowledge of a third party who is not qualified to receive them, is punished by imprisonment for five years and a fine of 5,000,000 francs.

Where the disclosure provided for in the preceding paragraph of this article was committed through carelessness or negligence, the person responsible is punished by imprisonment for three years and a fine of 2,000,000 francs.

In the cases provided for in the two paragraphs of this article, prosecution may only be brought upon complaint by the victim, his or her legal representative or his or her successors in title.

###### Article 322

23 : The act of carrying out or having carried out processing of personal data which is the subject of or intended to be the subject of a transfer to a State not appearing on the list of States having an adequate level of personal data protection, drawn up by the Personal Data Protection Authority, is punished by imprisonment for five years and a fine of 5,000,000 francs.

###### Article 322

24 : Whoever obstructs the action of the Personal Data Protection Authority is punished by imprisonment for three months and a fine of 120,000 francs:

1°) either by opposing the exercise of the missions entrusted to its members or to authorized agents pursuant to the law on personal data;

2°) either by refusing to communicate to its members or to authorized agents pursuant to the law on personal data, the information and documents useful for their mission, or by concealing said documents or information, or by causing them to disappear;

3°) either by communicating information which does not conform to the content of the records as it was at the time the request was made or which does not present that content in a directly accessible form.

###### Article 322

25 : In the cases provided for in articles 322-10 to 322-23 above, the erasure of all or part of the personal data which is the subject of the processing giving rise to the offence may be ordered. The commissioners and agents of the Personal Data Protection Authority are authorized to verify the erasure of such data.

###### Article 322

26 : Where such information is required by law, the act, for the person responsible for automated processing of personal data, is punished by imprisonment for three months and a fine of 120,000 francs:

1°) of not informing the person from whom personal data concerning him or her are collected:

a)	of the identity of the person responsible for the processing and, where applicable, that of his or her representative;

b)	of the purpose pursued by the processing for which the data are intended;

c)	of the mandatory or optional nature of the responses;

d)	of the possible consequences for him or her of a failure to respond;

e)	of the recipients or categories of recipients of the data;

f)	of his or her rights of opposition, inquiry, access and rectification;

g)	where applicable, of the transfers of personal data envisaged to a State not appearing on the list of countries having an adequate level of personal data protection;

2°) where the data are collected by means of a questionnaire, of not stating on the questionnaire the information relating to:

a)	the identity of the person responsible for the processing and, where applicable, that of his or her representative;

b)	the purpose pursued by the processing for which the data are intended;

c)	the mandatory or optional nature of the responses;

d)	the rights of opposition, inquiry, access and rectification of the persons from whom the data are collected;

3°) of not informing in a clear and precise manner any person using electronic communications networks:

a)	of the purpose of any action tending to access, by electronic transmission, information stored in his or her terminal connection equipment or to record, by the same means, information in his or her terminal connection equipment;

b)	of the means at his or her disposal to oppose it;

4°) of not providing to the person concerned, where the personal data have not been collected from him or her, the information listed in 1° and 2° from the time of recording the data or, if communication of the data to third parties is envisaged, at the latest at the time of the first communication of the data.

