12°) by coercion, threat or any other pressure, compels an official of the administration of the Land Registry and Cadastre services to create, to transfer a land title, or to register real rights on a land title, to abusively cancel a resolutory clause, or to act in violation of the provisions of the Land and Domain Code;

13°) acts in land matters in a domain where the law denies them any competence.

###### Article 415

5: Complicity in the above acts is punished as the offense itself.

###### Article 415

6: Constitutes the offense of forgery in land and domain matters and punished by imprisonment of ten years and a fine of 5,000,000 francs:

1°) the fraudulent alteration of land registers as well as the intentional use of said documents;

2°) the total or partial destruction of land registers;

3°) physical alterations intentionally caused with the aim of making impossible the use or exploitation of land registers.

###### Article 415

7: The offense of forgery indicated above is covered by the ten-year limitation period which begins to run from the commission of the acts.

###### Article 415

8: Constitutes the offense of criminal breach of trust and punished by the penalties of article 416-1 in fine of this Code, the act by a representative of public authority of disposing without allocation or without granted competence, of lands of the private immovable domain of the State.

###### Article 415

9: The discovery of an act or transfer subject to the provisions of this Code not presented to the land registry office for publication within the prescribed time limits is sanctioned by the application of a double fee in addition without this fee being less than double the fixed fees relating thereto.

