10: The voluntary presentation, outside the time limits, of acts subject to the publication formality is liable to an additional fee, without this fee being less than the amount of the fixed fees relating thereto.

###### Article 415

11: The person or parties who should have the publication formality carried out bear the penalties.

##### Section 3

Offenses in matters of checks, bank cards and other electronic payment instruments and processes

[Law No. 10-020 of 31 May 2010 establishing uniform law on offenses in matters of checks, bank cards and other electronic payment instruments and processes]

###### Paragraphe 1: Prosecution of offenses related to the use of checks

###### Article 415

12: Is punished by imprisonment of three years and a fine of 2,000,000 francs:

1°) the drawer or agent who, knowingly, issues a check domiciled on a closed account;

2°) the drawer who, after issuing a check, withdraws all or part of the provision, by transfer, wire transfer or any means whatsoever, with the intention of infringing the rights of others;

3°) the drawer who issues one or more checks in defiance of the injunction addressed to them pursuant to article 115 of the Regulation on payment systems in the Member States of the West African Economic and Monetary Union;

4°) the agent who, knowingly, issues one or more checks whose issuance is prohibited to their principal, pursuant to article 115 of the Regulation referred to above;

5°) any person who forbids the drawee to pay outside the cases provided for by article 84 paragraph 3 of the Regulation referred to above;

6°) any person who agrees to receive or endorse, knowingly, a check without provision;

7°) any person who, knowingly, makes use of a stolen check.

The attempt of the offenses listed above is punished as the completed offense.
The fine referred to in paragraph 1 may be increased to 5,000,000 francs if the drawer is a merchant or repeat offender.

###### Article 415

13: Is punished by imprisonment of five years and a fine of 5,000,000 francs:
1°) any person who counterfeits, falsifies or attempts to counterfeit or falsify a check;
2°) any person who knowingly, uses or attempts to use a counterfeited or falsified check;
3°) any person who, knowingly, agrees to receive a counterfeited or falsified check.

###### Article 415

14: Is punished by imprisonment of seven years and a fine of 10,000,000 francs anyone who knowingly, manufactures, acquires, possesses, transfers, offers or makes available materials, machines, apparatus, equipment, instruments, computer programs or any data designed or specially adapted to commit the offenses provided for in point 1 of article 415-13 above.
The attempt of the offenses listed above is punished as the completed offense.

###### Article 415

15: The confiscation, for purposes of destruction, of counterfeited or falsified checks, is mandatory in the cases provided for in articles 415-12 to 415-14 above.
Also mandatory is the confiscation of materials, machines, apparatus, equipment, instruments, computer programs or any data that serve or are intended to serve in the manufacture of said checks, except when they are used without the knowledge of the owner.

