##### Section 7: Offences relating to the liquidation of companies

###### Article 423

18: In application of Article 902 of the Uniform Act on the law of commercial companies and economic interest groups, any liquidator of a company who knowingly:

- within one month from his appointment, does not publish in a newspaper authorized to receive legal notices of the place of the registered office, the act appointing him liquidator and deposit with the Trade and Personal Property Credit Register the decisions pronouncing the dissolution;
- does not convene the members, at the end of the liquidation, to decide on the final account of the liquidation, on the discharge of his management and the release of his mandate and to record the closure of the liquidation;
- in the case provided for by Article 219 of the Uniform Act, does not deposit his final accounts at the registry of the Court responsible for commercial matters of the place of the registered office, nor request judicial approval thereof.

shall be punished by five years' imprisonment and a fine of 5,000,000 francs.

###### Article 423

19: In application of Article 903 of the Uniform Act on the law of commercial companies and economic interest groups, when the liquidation occurs by judicial decision, any liquidator who knowingly:

- within six months of the closure of his appointment, does not present a report on the assets and liabilities of the company in liquidation and on the continuation of liquidation operations, nor request the necessary authorizations to complete them;

- within three months of the closure of each financial year, does not prepare the summary financial statements in view of the inventory and a written report in which he accounts for the liquidation operations during the past financial year;
- does not allow the members to exercise, during the liquidation period, their right to access company documents under the same conditions as previously;
- does not convene the members at least once a year to report to them on the summary financial statements in case of continuation of the company's operations;
- does not deposit in an account opened in a bank in the name of the company in liquidation, within fifteen days from the distribution decision, the sums allocated to distributions among the members and creditors;
- does not deposit, in a consignment account opened in the books of the Public Treasury, within one year from the closure of the liquidation, the sums allocated to creditors or members and not claimed by them.

shall be punished by five years' imprisonment and a fine of 5,000,000 francs.

###### Article 423

20: In application of Article 904 of the Uniform Act on the law of commercial companies and economic interest groups, any liquidator who, in bad faith:

- makes use of the assets or credit of the company in liquidation in a manner he knows to be contrary to the interest of the company, for personal purposes or to favor another legal entity in which he has an interest, directly or indirectly;

- transfers all or part of the assets of the company in liquidation to a person having in the company the capacity of general partner, limited partner, manager, member of the board of directors, general administrator or auditor, without having obtained the unanimous consent of the members or, failing that, the authorization of the competent court.

shall be punished by five years' imprisonment and a fine of 20,000,000 francs.

##### Section 8

Offences relating to the failure to disclose information on the beneficial owners of legal entities and other legal arrangements

###### Article 423

21: In application of legislative and regulatory provisions on the obligation to disclose the beneficial owners of legal entities, designated shareholders and directors, managers and administrators of fiducies, trusts and other similar legal arrangements, as well as their directors, designated shareholders and directors, managers and administrators of fiducies, trusts and other similar legal arrangements who knowingly:

- fail to maintain and preserve adequate, accurate and up-to-date information on their own beneficial owners;

- do not file with the competent authorities the declaration of their beneficial owners or fail to update said declaration;

- do not make available to the competent authorities and reporting entities, without hindrance, in a timely manner, the above information;

- do not keep for ten years the registers of beneficial owners;

- do not disclose their status as designated director or candidate for such status;

- perform late or provide false declarations on beneficial owners.

- Shall be punished by the penalties provided for by the uniform law on combating money laundering and terrorist financing with regard to the identification of beneficial owners.

###### Article 423

22: The above criminal sanction applies without prejudice to the specific fines provided for by the texts establishing this obligation.

#### Chapter 4

Offences contained in the Uniform Act of 10 September 2015 on the organization of collective proceedings for the settlement of liabilities

##### Section 1: Bankruptcy and related offences

###### Article 424

1: In application of Article 227 of the Uniform Act on the organization of collective proceedings for the settlement of liabilities, the provisions of this section apply to traders, natural persons, and to members of commercial companies who have the status of trader.

###### Paragraph 1: Bankruptcy

###### Article 424

2: In application of Article 228 of the Uniform Act on the organization of collective proceedings for the settlement of liabilities, any trader, natural person, in a state of cessation of payments, who:

- contracts without receiving values in exchange, commitments deemed too large in view of his situation when he contracts them with the intention of delaying the finding of the cessation of his payments, makes purchases with a view to resale below the market price or if, with the same intention, employs ruinous means to procure funds;

- without legitimate excuse, does not make at the registry of the competent court, the declaration of his state of cessation of payments within thirty days;

- keeps incomplete or irregular accounts or does not keep them in accordance with accounting rules and recognized practices in the profession having regard to the size of the enterprise.

shall be declared guilty of simple bankruptcy and punished by two years' imprisonment.

The trader, natural person, is also guilty of bankruptcy and punished by the penalties provided for in paragraph 1 above when, after having been declared three times in a state of cessation of payments within five years, these proceedings have been closed for insufficiency of assets.

