###### Article 424

3: In application of Article 229 of the Uniform Act on collective proceedings for clearing liabilities, any natural person who, in the event of cessation of payments, is declared guilty of fraudulent bankruptcy and punished by ten years' imprisonment:

- conceals their accounts;

- misappropriates or dissipates all or part of their assets;

- fraudulently acknowledges being a debtor of sums they did not owe either in their books, or by public deeds or private written commitments, or in their balance sheet;

- exercises the commercial profession in violation of a prohibition provided for by the Uniform Acts or by law;

- after cessation of payments, pays a creditor to the detriment of the estate;

- stipulates with a creditor particular advantages by reason of their vote in the deliberations of the estate, or makes with a creditor a particular agreement from which results for the latter an advantage at the expense of the debtor's assets from the day of the opening decision.

Any merchant who is a natural person is also declared guilty of fraudulent bankruptcy and punished by the same penalty, who, on the occasion of a preventive settlement, judicial reorganization and liquidation of assets procedure:

- in bad faith, presents or causes to be presented a profit and loss account, a balance sheet, a statement of receivables or debts or an active and passive statement of privileges and securities, that is inaccurate or incomplete;

- without authorization from the president of the competent court, performs one of the acts prohibited by Article 11 of the Uniform Act on collective proceedings for clearing liabilities.

###### Paragraphe 2: Des infractions assimilées aux banqueroutes

###### Article 424

4: In application of Article 230 of the Uniform Act on collective proceedings for clearing liabilities, these provisions and those of Articles 424-5 and 424-6 below are applicable to natural persons who are directors of legal persons subject to collective proceedings and to their permanent representatives.

The directors referred to in this article mean all directors de jure or de facto and in general, any person having directly or through an intermediary, administered, managed or liquidated the legal person under cover of or in place of its legal representatives.

###### Article 424

5: In application of Article 231 of the Uniform Act on collective proceedings for clearing liabilities, the directors referred to in Article 424-4 above who, in that capacity and in bad faith, are punished by two years' imprisonment:

- consume sums belonging to the legal person by making purely speculative transactions or fictitious transactions;

- make purchases with a view to resale below market price or use ruinous means to procure funds with the intention of delaying the finding of cessation of payments of the legal person;

- pay or cause to be paid a creditor to the detriment of the estate after cessation of payments of the legal person;

- cause the legal person to contract on behalf of others, without receiving assets in exchange, commitments deemed too significant having regard to its situation when these were contracted;

- keep, cause to be kept or allow to be kept irregular or incomplete accounts of the legal person under the conditions provided for in Article 424-2 above;

- fail to make at the registry of the competent court, within thirty days, the declaration of the state of cessation of payments of the legal person.

###### Article 424

6: In application of Article 232 of the Uniform Act on collective proceedings for clearing liabilities, the legal or de facto representatives of legal persons comprising partners indefinitely and jointly liable for the debts thereof who, without legitimate excuse, do not make at the registry of the competent court the declaration of the state of cessation of payments within thirty days or if this declaration does not include the list of jointly liable partners with indication of their first names, surname and domicile, are declared guilty of simple bankruptcy and punished by two years' imprisonment.

###### Article 424

7: In application of Article 233 of the Uniform Act on collective proceedings for clearing liabilities, the directors referred to in Article 424-6 above who fraudulently are punished by ten years' imprisonment:

- misappropriate or conceal, attempt to misappropriate or conceal part of their assets or fraudulently acknowledge being debtors of sums they do not owe in order to remove all or part of their patrimony from the claims of the legal person in a state of cessation of payments or from those of the partners or creditors of the legal person in a state of cessation of payments;

- conceal the books of the legal person;

- misappropriate or conceal part of its assets;

- acknowledge the legal person as debtor of sums it does not owe, either in the books, or by public deeds or private written commitments, or in the balance sheet;

- exercise the profession of director contrary to a prohibition provided for by the uniform acts or by law;
- stipulate with a creditor, in the name of the legal person, particular advantages by reason of their vote in the deliberations of the estate or who conclude with a creditor a particular agreement from which results for the latter an advantage at the expense of the assets of the legal person from the day of the decision declaring cessation of payments.
The directors referred to in Article 424-6 above are also punished by the same penalty, who, on the occasion of collective proceedings:
- in bad faith, present or cause to be presented a profit and loss account, a balance sheet, a statement of receivables or debts or an active and passive statement of privileges and securities, that is inaccurate or incomplete;
- without authorization from the president of the competent court, perform one of the acts prohibited by Article 11 of the Uniform Act on collective proceedings for clearing liabilities.

##### Section 2: Des autres infractions

###### Article 424

8: In application of Article 240 of the Uniform Act on collective proceedings for clearing liabilities, the following are punished by ten years' imprisonment:
- persons convicted of having, in the interest of the debtor, removed, concealed or hidden all or part of the movable or immovable property, without prejudice to the application of criminal provisions relating to complicity;

- persons convicted of having fraudulently filed in the collective proceedings, either in their own name or through an intermediary or impersonation, fictitious claims;

- persons who, conducting business under the name of another or under a fictitious name, in bad faith, misappropriate, conceal, attempt to misappropriate or conceal part of their assets.

###### Article 424

9: In application of Article 241 of the Uniform Act on collective proceedings for clearing liabilities, the spouse, descendants, ascendants or collateral relatives of the debtor or their in-laws who, without the debtor's knowledge, misappropriate, divert or conceal assets forming part of the assets of the debtor in a state of cessation of payments, are punished by three years' imprisonment and a fine of 500,000 francs.

