##### Section 2: Criminal sanctions applicable to natural persons

###### Article 431

2: Natural persons guilty of a money laundering offence are punished by seven years' imprisonment and a fine equal to three times the value of the property or funds that were the subject of the laundering operations.

Attempted money laundering is punished by the same penalties.

##### Section 3

Criminal sanctions applicable to conspiracy, association, complicity with a view to money laundering

###### Article 431

3: Conspiracy or participation in an association with a view to committing an act constituting money laundering, association to commit said act, assistance, incitement or advice to a natural or legal person, with a view to executing it or facilitating its execution are punished by the same penalties provided for in Article 431-2 above.

##### Section 4: Aggravating circumstances

###### Article 431

4: The penalties provided for in Article 431-2 above are doubled:

1°) when the money laundering offence is committed habitually or by using facilities provided by the exercise of a professional activity;

2°) when the perpetrator of the offence is a repeat offender. In this case, convictions pronounced abroad are taken into account to establish recidivism;

3°) when the money laundering offence is committed by an organized gang.

When the crime or offence from which the property or sums of money that were the subject of the money laundering offence originates is punished by a custodial sentence of a duration greater than that of the imprisonment incurred under Article 431-2 above, the money laundering is punished by the penalties attached to the original offence of which its perpetrator had knowledge and, if this offence is accompanied by aggravating circumstances, by the penalties attached only to the circumstances of which he had knowledge.

##### Section 5: Criminal sanctions for certain acts related to money laundering

###### Article 431

5: Persons and directors or agents of natural or legal persons referred to in Articles 5 and 6 of the uniform law on combating money laundering and the financing of terrorism are punished by two years' imprisonment and a fine of 1,500,000 francs, when the latter have intentionally:

1°) made disclosures to the owner of the sums or to the perpetrator of the operations referred to in Article 431-1 above concerning the declaration they are required to make or the action taken thereon;

2°) destroyed or removed documents or papers relating to the identification obligations referred to in Articles 26 to 31 whose retention is provided for by Article 35 of said law;
3°) carried out or attempted to carry out under a false identity one of the operations referred to in Articles 32, 33 and 39 to 45 and 53 of said law;

4°) informed by any means the person(s) covered by the investigation conducted for money laundering offences of which they became aware by reason of their profession or functions;

5°) communicated to the judicial authorities or to the officials competent to establish the original and subsequent offences the acts and documents referred to in Article 89 of said law, which they know to be falsified or erroneous;

6°) communicated information or documents to persons other than those referred to in Article 36 of said law;

7°) failed to make the suspicious transaction report provided for in Article 79 of said law, when the circumstances led to the conclusion that the sums of money could originate from a money laundering offence as defined in Article 7 of said law.

Persons and directors or agents of natural or legal persons referred to in Articles 5 and 6 of said law are punished by a fine of 750,000 francs, when the latter have unintentionally:

-	failed to make the suspicious transaction report provided for in Article 79 of said law;

-	contravened the provisions of Articles 16, 18 to 40 and 79 of said law.

##### Section 6

Optional additional criminal sanctions applicable to natural persons

###### Article 431

6: Natural persons guilty of the offences defined in Articles 431-1 to 431-5 above may also incur the following additional penalties:

1°) prohibition from residing in the national territory for a period of five years, pronounced against any convicted foreigner;

2°) prohibition from residing for a period of five years in one or more administrative districts;

3°) prohibition from leaving the national territory and withdrawal of passport for a period of three years;

4°) prohibition from exercising civil and political rights for a period of three years;

5°) prohibition from driving motorized land, sea and air vehicles and withdrawal of driving permits or licenses for a period of six years;

6°) permanent or six-year prohibition from exercising the profession or activity in connection with which the offence was committed and prohibition from exercising a public function;

7°) prohibition from issuing cheques other than those that allow the withdrawal of funds by the drawer from the drawee or those that are certified and prohibition from using payment cards for six years;

8°) prohibition from holding or carrying a weapon subject to authorization for six years;

9°) confiscation of all or part of the convicted person's property of lawful origin;

10°) confiscation of the property or thing that was used or intended to commit the offence or the thing that is the product thereof, with the exception of objects that may be returned.

##### Section 7: Exclusion of benefit of suspended sentence

###### Article 431

7: No criminal sanction pronounced for a money laundering offence may be accompanied by a suspended sentence.

