###### Article 551

15: Without prejudice to the application of amnesty laws, information relating to judicial convictions and administrative measures affecting the driving licence must be erased in accordance with the statutory limitation period without a new judicial decision or a measure mentioned in paragraph 3 of Article 551-13 above having intervened.

The period provided for in the preceding paragraph runs:

1°) for judicial convictions, from the day on which the last conviction became final;

2°) for administrative measures, from the day of the last decision.

In the case where an administrative measure is annulled, the erasure of information relating to that measure is carried out on the day of the judicial or administrative decision pronouncing that annulment.

The period is extended to ten years from the day on which the conviction became final when paragraph 3 of Article 551-11 above is applied.

The period is reduced to two years from the day of registration for information relating to driving licences for which issuance is requested.

###### Article 551

16: The holder of the driving licence has the right to communication of the complete record of entries concerning him or her. He or she may not obtain a copy thereof.

###### Article 551

17: The complete record of entries relating to licences applicable to the same person is issued at their request to:

1°) the judicial authorities;

2°) Judicial Police Officers responsible for executing a court order or acting within the framework of a flagrante delicto investigation.

###### Article 551

18: Information relating to the existence, category and validity of the driving licence is communicated at their request to:

1°) the holder of the licence, his or her lawyer or his or her representative;

2°) the competent foreign authorities, for the purposes of authentication of the driving licence in accordance with international agreements in force;

3°) Judicial Police Officers acting within the framework of a preliminary investigation;

4°) Gendarmes and Military Personnel of the National Police authorised to carry out road checks in application of regulations relating to road traffic;

5°) civil and military administrative authorities for persons employed or likely to be employed as drivers of motor land vehicles;

6°) insurance companies for persons whose liability they guarantee or are called upon to guarantee incurred as a result of damage caused by motor land vehicles.

###### Article 551

19: Information, other than that mentioned in Article 551-19 below relating to administrative documents required for the circulation of vehicles, is communicated at their request to:
1°) the natural or legal person holding the administrative documents, his or her lawyer or his or her representative;
2°) the judicial authorities;
3°) Judicial Police Officers in the exercise of their mission defined in the Code of Criminal Procedure;
4°) Gendarmes and Military Personnel of the National Police authorised to carry out road checks in application of regulations relating to road traffic;

5°) officials authorised to record offences against traffic police regulations for the sole purpose of identifying the perpetrators of such offences;

6°) the authorities of Territorial Collectivities for the exercise of their competence in matters of vehicle circulation;

7°) the services of the Ministry in charge of Industry for the exercise of their competences;

8°) insurance companies guaranteeing damage suffered by third parties resulting from harm to persons or property in the occurrence of which a motor land vehicle, as well as its trailers or semi-trailers are involved and organisations assimilated to these companies provided that such information has the sole purpose of identifying the property or persons involved in a traffic accident on condition that at least one of the vehicles is insured by the applicant or that the latter is responsible for compensating one of the victims.

Insurance companies must provide in support of their request all useful elements making it possible to verify the reality of the loss.

###### Article 551

20: Information relating, on the one hand to pledges constituted on motor land vehicles and, on the other hand to oppositions to the transfer of the registration certificate, is communicated at their request to:

1°) the natural or legal person holding the administrative documents, his or her lawyer or his or her representative;

2°) the judicial authorities;

3°) Judicial Police Officers in the exercise of their mission defined in the Code of Criminal Procedure;

4°) the authorities of Territorial Collectivities for the exercise of their powers in matters of vehicle use and circulation on public roads.

The absence of a declaration of pledge or opposition made to the transfer of the certificate of a vehicle defined by its registration number alone may, to the exclusion of any other information, be brought to the attention of any other person who requests it.

###### Article 551

21: Information relating to the civil status of the holder of the registration certificate, the registration number and the characteristics of the vehicle, as well as pledges constituted and oppositions are, to the exclusion of any other information, communicated at their request for their mission to:

1°) agents responsible for executing an enforceable instrument;

2°) judicial administrators and liquidators or trustees appointed within the framework of a judicial reorganisation or liquidation of assets procedure provided for by the Commercial Code.

###### Article 551

22: No nominative information may be disclosed outside the cases provided for in Articles 551-15 and 551-21 above.

###### Article 551

23: Any person who is punished by the penalties provided for by this Code:

1°) takes the name of a person in circumstances which have determined or which could have determined the registration in the name of that person of a judicial conviction or an administrative decision;

2°) obtains communication, by taking a false name or a false capacity, of the record of entries registered concerning a third party;

3°) obtains, either directly or indirectly, communication of nominative information the disclosure of which is not expressly provided for by the law relating to road traffic.

[Law No. 029 of 29 June 2006, as amended, relating to the protection of public roads]

###### Article 551

24: Any person who contravenes the provisions of Article 5 of the law relating to the protection of public roads is punished by imprisonment of six months and a fine of 200,000 francs, after a formal notice without follow-up from the competent authority.

###### Article 551

25: Any person who erects or orders the erection without authorisation from the competent authorities of a speed bump on the public road is punished by imprisonment of thirty days and a fine of 200,000 francs.

