###### Paragraph 1: Offences relating to road traffic policing

[Decree No. 2023-0509 PT-RM of 12 September 2023 establishing the conditions for the use of roads open to public traffic and the putting into circulation of vehicles]

###### Article 602

2: Any person who contravenes the obligation to immobilise the vehicle or the injunctions addressed to them by agents authorised to record offences relating to road traffic policing, in particular for offences related to vehicle equipment or when the driver or their load causes damage to the road or its appurtenances, is punished by a fine of 15,000 francs.

###### Article 602

3: Any person who offers for sale or sells a vehicle or trailer in violation of the provisions relating to vehicle registration is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs.

###### Article 602

4: Any driver of a vehicle who knowingly fails to comply with an order to stop issued by an agent responsible for recording offences and wearing the external and visible insignia of their capacity, or who refuses to submit to the prescribed legal checks concerning the vehicle or its driver, is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs.

###### Article 602

5: Any person who has contravened the provisions concerning the following is punished by a fine of 15,000 francs:

a)	directions imposed on traffic;

b)	passing and overtaking;

c)	the speed of motor vehicles with or without trailers;

d)	road intersections and right of way;

e)	significant changes of direction;

f)	parking outside built-up areas when visibility is insufficient near a road intersection, at the top of a hill or on a bend, or at night in unlit places;

g)	the use of lighting, signalling and advance signalling devices outside the cases of change of direction provided for in the provisions of the decree establishing the conditions for the use of roads open to public traffic and the putting into circulation of vehicles;

h)	level crossings;

i)	working conditions in road transport;

j)	signals prescribing a complete stop;

k)	prohibitions or restrictions on traffic provided for on certain routes for certain categories of vehicles or for vehicles carrying out certain transport;

l)	obligations or prohibitions relating to the use of roads with specialised traffic;

m)	traffic restrictions enacted on the occasion of races and sporting events;

n)	the wearing of protective helmets concerning drivers and passengers of motorcycles, mopeds and motorised bicycles;

o)	stopping or parking in any place where they would constitute a danger;

p)	the transport, for commercial purposes or otherwise, of a number of persons exceeding that which the vehicle used is authorised to carry on board;

q)	the use of a device equipped with a screen placed in the field of vision of the driver of a vehicle in motion and not constituting a driving or navigation aid.

Any person who commits a new offence against the provisions regulating parking in built-up areas when they have, in the six months preceding this offence, committed in the same built-up area at least two offences of the same nature followed by conviction is punished by a fine of 15,000 francs.

The fine is increased to the maximum when the number of offences previously committed under the same conditions is at least four. This same penalty is incurred from the second conviction in the cases referred to in paragraph 1 of this article.

###### Article 602

6: Any person who has contravened the provisions concerning the following is punished by a fine of 5,000 francs:

a)	the driving of vehicles and animals, including parking and stopping, outside the cases provided for in the other articles of the decree establishing the conditions for the use of roads open to public traffic and the putting into circulation of vehicles;

b)	the speed of animals and vehicles without a motor with or without a trailer or semi-trailer;

c)	the use of audible warning devices;

d)	the wearing of seat belts and the transport of children provided for in the provisions relating to the equipment of vehicle users referred to in the decree cited above.

###### Article 602

7: Any person who has contravened the rules concerning the regulations on rain barriers and the crossing of bridges is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs.

In the event of a repeat offence, the fine is doubled.

###### Article 602

8: Any person who has contravened the provisions concerning the following is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs:

a)	the organisation of races and sporting events;

b)	the crossing of ferries.

When the fault, negligence or imprudence of a user has caused damage to a public road or its appurtenances, said user is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs, without prejudice, where applicable, to the more severe penalties provided for by Article 602-1-4 of this Code. They are, in addition, sentenced to reimbursement of repair costs for the benefit of the State or the Territorial Authority that suffered the damage.

###### Article 602

9: Any person who, having placed on a road open to public traffic or in its immediate vicinity an object or device likely to cause a disturbance to traffic, does not comply with the injunctions addressed with a view to the removal of said object or device, by one of the agents authorised to record offences relating to road traffic, is punished by a fine of 15,000 francs.

###### Article 602

10: Any person who contravenes the special provisions of the decree cited above concerning pedestrian traffic is punished by a fine of 5,000 francs.

###### Article 602

11: Without prejudice to the requirements of the law governing road traffic, any person who contravenes the provisions of the decree cited above concerning the following is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs:

a)	the brakes of motor vehicles other than motorcycles and mopeds;

b)	the number of authorised seats for public passenger transport vehicles;

c)	the speedometer.

In the event of new offences committed by the same person, a fine of 18,000 francs is imposed.

Any carrier or vehicle owner who contravenes the provisions adopted by joint order of the minister responsible for Transport, the minister responsible for Security and the minister responsible for Finance concerning the control of axle load of vehicles, is punished according to the case by the following penalties:

Overload of 1 to 5 tonnes ——————5,000 francs per tonne

Overload of 6 to 10 tonnes —————10,000 francs per tonne

Overload of 11 to 15 tonnes —————15,000 francs per tonne Overload of more than 15 tonnes————18,000 francs per tonne

###### Article 602

12: Any person who contravenes, except those mentioned in the preceding article, the following is punished by a fine of 15,000 francs:

1°) the particular provisions applicable to motor vehicles and vehicle combinations;

2°) the particular provisions applicable to agricultural vehicles and machinery and to certain special equipment;

3°) the particular provisions applicable to motorcycles, mopeds, tricycles and quadricycles with a motor and their trailers.

However, offences concerning bicycles and their equipment expose their perpetrators to a fine of 5,000 francs.

