###### Article 602

13: Without prejudice to subsequent justification of possession of the document or documents not presented, any person who was unable to immediately present during a roadside check one of the documents listed below is punished by a fine of 3,000 francs:

1. their driving licence or driving permit;
2. the vehicle registration certificate and, where applicable, that of the trailer or semi-trailer or the provisional receipts;
3. the insurance certificate provided for by the Treaty establishing an integrated organization of the insurance industry in African States;
4. the special technical inspection certificate;
5. where applicable:
- the exceptional transport authorization;
- the public transport authorization;
- the authorization to operate a taxi or a hire car with driver;
- the route sheet relating to a hire car without driver;
- the road crossing fee ticket;
- the consignment note.
Any person who, invited to justify within a period of ten days possession of the authorizations and documents mentioned in the first paragraph, has not presented these documents before the expiry of this period is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs.

###### Article 602

14: Without prejudice to the more severe penalties applicable to offences against the rules concerning the driving of vehicles, vehicles and their equipment, any person who is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs:

a) causes to circulate on roads open to public traffic a motor vehicle or a towed vehicle without registration plates or the external markings required by this Code;

b) voluntarily puts or keeps in circulation a motor vehicle or towed vehicle fitted with plates or markings not corresponding to the type of vehicle or to that of the user;

c) puts or keeps in circulation a motor vehicle or towed vehicle without holding the authorizations or administrative documents required for the circulation of this vehicle or who has not presented said vehicle for technical inspection within the regulatory time limits;

d) makes use of authorizations or administrative documents required for the circulation of a motor vehicle or towed vehicle which they know to be expired or cancelled;

e) drives a vehicle without having applied for the extension of their driving licence or driving permit, or without having complied with the conditions of validity thereof.

###### Paragraphe 2

Traffic offences contained in Decree No. 2019-0590/P-RIM of 31 July 2019 establishing the rules applicable to navigation and transport on navigable waterways in the Republic of Mali

###### Article 602

15: Any person who contravenes the provisions concerning is punished by a fine of 15,000 francs:

- the directions imposed on navigation;

- the requirements relating to the registration of craft;

- compliance with the useful load of the craft;

- general documents;

- the rules of use relating to the safety of the craft, persons on board and their property;

- the use of lighting and signalling devices outside the cases provided for in the decree establishing the rules applicable to navigation and transport on navigable waterways in the Republic of Mali.

###### Article 602

16: Failure to present one of the authorizations or administrative documents required for the navigation of a boat or motorized craft is punished by a fine of 3,000 francs.

Any person who, invited to justify within a period of ten days possession of the authorizations or administrative documents mentioned above, does not present these documents before the expiry of this period is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs.

###### Article 602

17: Without prejudice to the provisions of this Code, any person who is punished by a fine of 18,000 francs:

a) causes to navigate on navigable waterways, apart from small craft, a motorized craft without registration plates;

b) voluntarily puts or keeps in navigation, apart from small craft, a motorized craft fitted with plates or markings not corresponding to the type of craft or to that of the user;

c) puts or keeps in navigation, apart from small craft, a motorized craft without holding the authorizations or administrative documents required for the navigation of this boat or who has not presented said boat for technical inspection within the regulatory time limits;

d) makes use of authorizations or administrative documents required for the navigation of a motorized craft which they knew to be expired or cancelled;

e) operates a boat without having applied for the extension of their licence or navigation permit, or without having complied with the conditions of validity thereof.
